            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mymeshell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a true Mojito! A must have recipe-I spend most of my summers in and around the Carribean, this drink always takes me back there!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mark Krosse"
            },
            "reviewBody": "authentic variations - (ht to Key West Legal Rum Distillery)\n\n1/ two tsp (or 3, or 4) of turbinado / demerara sugar - imparts a molasses hint\n2/ KEY LIMES, eg key lime juice - imparts a more intense lime experience - see Kermit's or other\n3/ mint with their stems - stems have more mint oil than just leaves\n\navoid the slice of lime - the white pulp is extra bitter\n\nmuddle 20 times - no more, no less\n\nuse a long thin spoon, not a straw - the Mojito experience is to continue to work/remix the ingredients up &amp; down as you savor it",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-01T20:05:42.900Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made these and man, they were so good! Another person complained that they weren't sweet enough so i added a little more sugar. I used a mortar and pestle to grind up the sugar, lime wedge, and mint leaves and then i put it into the glass, added the rum and the soda water. The store didnt have club soda, but they had seltzer water, no problem with that. I crushed up my ice in a blender. I only had dark rum, so i used that, no problem. Just taste it as you go, to see if you have enough lime or sugar or mint leaves, to your liking. I added an additional mint leaf to each drink. Amazon has all those mortar and pestle grinders or wooden muddlers for stuff like this. You do have to use something to grind the mint leaves and lime wedges up, though. A spoon doesn't do the trick. You have to make these!!. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-10T00:18:23.847Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HandySalt1714"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Almost perfect! I learned in Habana to use powdered sugar (heaping tablespoon each glass) &amp; lots more mint!! Good w/ Lime Perrier instead of Club Soda. Very refreshing!!",
            "datePublished": "2023-08-17T23:06:15.318Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TopChef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For each Mojito, I use half a lime muddled with 1 tsp (or 2, if you like it sweet) sugar and 12 mint leaves. Then add 1 shot rum to a glass, 3 shots club soda, and mix with the muddled mixture. This does not have nearly enough mint for my taste.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-08T07:41:05.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessi Wynelle Tallent"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I also squeeze in some fresh orange juice. also for a little extra zing try a splash of ginger ale instead of club soda. I find club soda has a horrible after taste.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-17T21:07:00.767Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
